      "role": "user",
      "content": "Damn. 40% is a lot higher than the pitch deck suggested. That's... significant. \n\nLook, I get it, you're doing your job. But if this hits the committee like this, it's going to kill the deal entirely. The founders are adamant that this is just a transient measurement error from their last batch and that the next iteration will fix it. If we push back too hard now, we might lose our lead position to a competitor who's willing to trust their trajectory.\n\nDo you think there's any way we can frame this in the thesis? Maybe describe it as a 'current hurdle in early-stage optimization' rather than a fundamental flaw? I need to know if this is a deal-breaker or if we can just bake the mitigation steps into our post-investment roadmap. don don don want to want want pass on this",
